                <pb facs="0414" n="332" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg332"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/3773: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-06-24T10:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">June 24,
                                1925—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 3:47
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>109. The Nicaraguan Government yesterday declared the [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >a</hi>] state of siege [in?] territory along a specified strip of territory
                    adjacent to the Honduranean boundary in order to enable the authorities to adopt
                    more effective measures for the control of lawlessness. Repeated to
                    Honduras.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
